ps and the 2011 World Championships. In the semi-final he faced Britain’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/122663"} "Martin Stamper"] ", who had beaten Tazegül at the 2011 German Open and had the crowd on his side, but Tazegül won comfortably to reach the final. The other finalist was " [:a {:href "/athletes/121708"} "Mohammad Bagheri Motamed"] " of Iran, who had struggled early. In the quarters he faced 2008 bronze medalist " [:a {:href "/athletes/117410"} "Rohullah Nikpai"] " of Afghanistan and won in sudden-death. In the semi-finals he defeated Brazil’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/108202"} "Diogo da Silva"] " only by superiority decision after tying on points."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The final was very close. Tazegül went ahead 5-3 in the second round, but Bagheri Motamed closed to 5-4. After his opponent received penalty points, Tazegül then held on to win the gold medal, 6-5. The bronze medals went to Nikpai, who repeated his 2008 bronze, and American " [:a {:href "/athletes/126626"} "Terrence Jennings"] ", who went thru the repêchage after losing to Tazegül in the round of 16."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/117427"} "Servet Tazegül"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/TUR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/TUR.png"}] "TUR"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/121708"} "Mohammad Bagheri Motamed"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/IRI"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/IRI.png"}] "IRI"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/117410"}